<title>BELGIUM: EU cereals experts to consider extra millet quota.</title>
<headline>EU cereals experts to consider extra millet quota.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Union cereals experts will discuss an implementing regulation on Thursday covering an additional import quota of about 1,000 tonnes of millet, an EU official said.</p>
<p>The quota was required under world trade rules covering the accession of Austria, which traditionally imported about 1,000 tonnes of millet, the official said.</p>
<p>The item could be put to a vote at the cereals management committee following the meeting of experts.</p>
</text>
